      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranchita%2C_California",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s original name was Cañada de la Verruga, Spanish for \"Valley of the Wart,\" used by Spaniards and Native Americans.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranchita%2C_California",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "William Johnson Helm built an adobe house west of present‑day Ranchita, and the area was later called \"Wid Helm's place.\".",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
